This directory is intentionally tracked (even when empty) so it always
exists as a valid Tauri bundle resource path -- see tauri.conf.json's
bundle.resources and the "Fetch optional bundled runtime assets" step in
.github/workflows/build-release.yml. When the KDEV_RUNTIME_ASSETS_URL
repository variable is set, CI populates this directory with real
interpreter/tool binaries before the build, laid out per runtime/README.md
(the top-level one, which documents the expected structure). When unset,
this directory stays empty and KDev falls back to reporting tools as
host-provided or missing, as runtime.rs already does honestly.
